ch & Discovery\nResearch at LSU New Orleans\nStudent Research\nStudy Abroad\nInternational Center\nFaculty & Staff Research\nCollaborate with LSU New Orleans\nOffice of Research\nA\nAcademic Resources\nCourse Catalog\nRegistrar Office\nAcademic Calendar\nAbout\nA\nAbout Us\nMission & Vision\nHistory\nAt a Glance\nCurrent Rankings\nLooking for UNO?\nA\nLeadership & Offices\nOffice of the President\nAdministrative Offices\nUniversity Advancement\nWork at LSU New Orleans\nNews\nA\nCommunity & Engagement\nAlumni\nFor Parents\nService Learning\nMake a Gift\nA\nPolicies & Safety\nTitle IX\nCampus Safety\nNon Discriminatory Policy\nAccessibility\nA\nUniversity Resources\nContact LSU New Orleans\nCampus Map\nAlumni\nMake a Gift\nFor Faculty & Staff\nPrivateer Athletics\nExplore the shop and see upcoming games.\nStudent Life\nA\nStudent Life\nResidential Life\nApply for Housing\nDining Services\nHousing Rates\nPontchartrain Halls\nLafitte Village\nCampus Recreation\nA\nGet Involved\nStudent Organizations\nStudent Involvement & Leadership\nGreek Life\nFirst Year Experience\nService Learning\nSocial Media\nInternational Center\nA\nHealth & Wellness\nCampus Health Services\nTitle IX Resources\nStudent Accountability\nA\nCareer & Success\nCareer Services\nStudent & Alumni Resources\nResearch Opportunities\nStudy Abroad\nAcademic Advising\nGraduation Information\nA\nStudent Resources\nCampus Map\nTranscript Request\nThe Dock\nPrivateer Athletics\nExplore the shop and see upcoming games.\nAthletics\nvisit\nvisit\nvisit\napply\napply\napply\nSearch\nvisit\nvisit\nvisit\napply\napply\napply\nEdit Page\nSkip to main content\nLSU New Orleans\nAcademics\nGraduate School | Graduate Degree Programs\nGraduate Financing\nFinancing Your Education\nInvesting in your future\nThe Graduate School is happy that you have selected LSU New Orleans to further your academic pursuits. We realize that your decision to enroll in a graduate degree program is an investment in your future. The Graduate School is committed to supporting you in this endeavor. These pages outline financial resources, either within or outside the University that may be available to you.How To Make A Payment\nResources\nOffice Of Financial Aid\nTuition And Fees\nCareer Compass Job Search Assistance\nIN THIS SECTION\nGraduate School\nAdmission Requirements\nDegree Programs\nAccelerated Masters Programs\nGraduate Student Resources\nFinancing Your Education\nGraduate FAQs\nNew Student Checklist\nContact Us\nGraduate School Scholarships\nGraduate School Awards: The Graduate School provides scholarships to incoming graduate students based on nomination of graduate coordinators.\nScholarship Nomination Form (faculty and staff only) Nominations are currently closed.\nFunding is also provided through schools and departments. Contact your program for more information.\nGraduate Assistantships\nGraduate Assistants work either 10 or 20 hours a week in a department on campus. Check with your program for availability. Click here for more detailed information.\nGRANT RESOURCE CENTER (GRC):\nSee the Office of Research\u2019s attached newsletter. (Weekly newsletters are archived on the Funding Opportunities page.) Several funding opportunity databases available for LSU New Orleans students. Additional information available here. Instructions and links to the funding databases are found here.\nFinancial Resources\nSee what other financial resources are available to help you finance your education.\nCareer Services Database: Career Services utilizes the Handshake platform to automate the connection process for student and employer profiles, resume and cover letter uploads, job postings, internship/apprenticeship/cooperative experiences, and register for career events tailored to YOUR career interests.\nMusic Awards: awarded to students pursuing a Masters of Music (MM). Contact Department of Music for more information.\nExternal Sources: LSU New Orleans subscribes to databases allowing you to search for funding opportunities. Some require LSU New Orleans IP address.\nGrantforward: Extensive database with grants from federal, corporate, and foundation sources.\nGRAPES: UCLA Graduate & Postdoctoral Extramural Support database\nNSF: National Science Foundation funding search\nFederal Student Aid: Federal resources for graduate students\nNRC Research Associateship Programs\nThe National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine maintain a database of more than 1,600 research opportunities and administer postdoctoral and senior research awards at participating federal laboratories and affiliated institutions at locations throughout the U.S. and abroad.\nMarine Studies Scholarships\nEach year, MTS awards funding to outstanding undergraduate and graduate students who are accepted into or enrolled in full-time marine-related programs, with a focus on marine technology, marine engineering, or marine science. Learn more and apply!\nFinancial Aid\nIf you have questions about your Federal Financial Aid, please contact your Financial Aid counselor.\nFooter\nContact\n2000 Lakeshore Drive New Orleans, LA 70148\n[email protected]\n[email protected]\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (888) 514-4275\n+1 (504) 384-7924\n+1 (504) 384-7924\nLearn\nAdmission information\nPrograms of study\nScholarships and awards\nTuition and fees\nGraduate programs\nFinancial aid\nImportant dates & deadlines\nExperience\nInternational center\nOur campus\nStudent life\nHousing\nCareer services\nAlumni\nMake a gift\nAnnual Security Report\nConnect\nAll social\nUniversity calendar\nNews\nFor parents\nEspanol - Tieng Viet\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nNon-Discrimination\nTitle IX\nCampus Crime\nEmergency Preparedness\n\u00a9 2026 LSU New Orleans. All Rights Reserved.", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/academics/grad/graduate-financing#main"], ["", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/"], ["", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/admissions"], ["Admissions", "https://www.lsuneworleans.edu/adm